* LT3045-1 Low-Dropout Regulator Stage : 5V IN -> 3.3V OUT @ 100mA
* -----------------------------------------------------------------
* Behavioral LT3045-1 macromodel (precision 100uA SET reference,
* error amplifier, low-dropout pass element).
* Vout = 100uA * Rset  ->  Rset = 33k  ->  Vout = 3.3V
* -----------------------------------------------------------------

*** Input source ***
V1 IN 0 DC 5

*** Input capacitor ***
Cin IN 0 10u
Rcin_esr IN 0 1G          ; keeps node well defined (negligible leakage)

*** Regulator ***
XU1 IN OUT SET LT3045_1

*** Output voltage programming resistor (100uA * 33k = 3.3V) ***
Rset SET 0 33k
Cset SET 0 10n            ; reference noise-reduction capacitor

*** Output capacitor ***
Cout OUT 0 10u
Resr OUT OUTX 5m
Vsense OUTX 0 0           ; ESR return path (0V, no effect on DC)

*** 100 mA resistive load (3.3V / 33ohm = 100mA) ***
Rload OUT 0 33

* -----------------------------------------------------------------
* LT3045-1 behavioral subcircuit
* Pins:  1=IN  2=OUT  3=SET
* -----------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt LT3045_1 IN OUT SET
* 100uA precision current reference sourced out of the SET pin
Iset IN SET 100u
* Error amplifier (transconductance stage + compensation cap)
Gea 0 CTL VALUE={1m*(V(SET)-V(OUT))}
Cea CTL 0 100n
Rea CTL 0 1G
* Pass device: follows CTL, clamped by input rail minus dropout (~250mV)
Bpass PDRV 0 V=limit(V(CTL),0,V(IN)-0.25)
Rpass PDRV OUT 20m
* Quiescent current
Iq IN 0 2.3m
.ends LT3045_1

* -----------------------------------------------------------------
* Analysis
* -----------------------------------------------------------------
.tran 10u 5m 0 10u
.meas TRAN vout_dc AVG V(OUT) FROM=4m TO=5m
.meas TRAN iload  AVG I(Rload) FROM=4m TO=5m
.options plotwinsize=0
.end
